WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.890
Week 4: Identity, Origin, Numbers, and Time. state origin and profession exchange contact numbers tell dates and times

2
00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:22.391
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can state origin and profession, exchange contact numbers, tell dates and times. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:22.391 --> 00:00:30.470
Language system. Ser for identity and origin; cardinal numbers; dates; telling time with es la and son las.

4
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:37.568
Sound and delivery. Tap r between vowels; distinguish pero from perro without exaggeration.

5
00:00:37.568 --> 00:00:47.101
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:47.101 --> 00:01:09.113
Model language. Soy de los Estados Unidos. — I am from the United States. Mi apellido es Clark. — My last name is Clark. Hoy es el diecinueve de julio. — Today is July nineteenth. Son las tres y cuarto. — It is a quarter past three. ¿A qué hora es la reunión? — What time is the meeting?

7
00:01:09.113 --> 00:01:19.118
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
